{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "_data": []}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n2le01ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe7n2le01ob02re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n2le01ob02re2img01.jpg", "text": "<strong>Carlos</strong>: Good afternoon, Ana. </br>\n<strong>Ana</strong>: Hi, Carlos. </br>\n<strong>Carlos</strong>: Are you Ok? </br>\n<strong>Ana</strong>: Well, I have to write a paper about programming for tomorrow, but I don't understand very well the concept. </br>\n<strong>Carlos</strong>: Why? Can I help you? I am a systems engineer. </br>\n<strong>Ana</strong>: I'm reading my textbook about programming, but the author doesn't define clearly what programming is. </br>\n<strong>Carlos</strong>: There are many postures related to the concept of programming, but the best definition is that programming is the action of lengthening, modifying, and generating the functionality of a system. Both specialists and non-specialists are able to program. </br>", "time": "100"}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n2le01ob02re2img02.jpg", "text": "<strong>Ana</strong>: That's  where I get confused. Are you saying that everybody can program? </br>\n<strong>Carlos</strong>: Yes, for example, your smartphone; the act of setting a language for your smartphone involves programming; even the act of activating my alarm clock is programming a device. This is broadly the definition of programming. </br>\n<strong>Ana</strong>: I understand, but I want to know, more technically, what programming is. </br>\n<strong>Carlos</strong>: For specialized people, programming refers to the setting steps for a program to run and fulfill certain specifications; in other words, programming aims to design the architecture of a program and codify it in a suitable programming language. Programming involves both a scientific part and a technical part; the architectural design of a program reflects its scientific conceptualization; while the codification of a program's design represents its technical definitions. </br>", "time": "39200"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n2le01ob02re2img03.jpg", "text": "<strong>Ana</strong>: So, programming is not all about learning the most common programming languages. </br>\n<strong>Carlos</strong>: Exactly! Depending on your design, you use a particular kind of language; for example, social-media application programmers use more complex languages, thus to ease the use of the application; on the other hand, system programmers don't interfere directly with end users, so they have more knowledge of core languages and technical aspects.", "time": "101500"}]}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"content": 1, "type": "template_override"}]}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "img_path": "", "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can identify the concept of computer programming.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can understand the concept of computer programming. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can exchange information about computer programming.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "In your opinion, what is the usefulness of programming systems? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Do you know how to design the architecture of a program? Explain. ", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"con