: [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "enpe7n2le01ob02re7pdf01.pdf", "type": "pdf"}], "type": "question"}]}], "stimuli_ids": [], "template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Make your own concept map about computer programming!", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Take Away", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}], "type": "post_instructions"}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}], "type": "lab_options"}]}], "type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "What is Programming?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 1, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A1.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about programming.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Understand key information about the concepts, principles, and methodologies in simple spoken and written situations.  Talk about programming techniques, use cases, kinds, and sequences in simple spoken and written situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures.  Identifies general aspects related to Software Programming in short written or spoken conversations about past experiences.", "type": "secondary_1"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Verbs + infinitive: Need to and Have to in Affirmative", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use a verb in infinitive after some verbs to express the purpose of an action.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are verbs that are followed by another action in the infinitive form to express purpose.</br> </br>   For example: </br> I <strong>need to send</strong> some information. </br> We <strong>have to buy</strong> a new program. </br> She <strong>wants to sell</strong> her computer. </br></br>  Notice that we conjugate the first verb depending on the subject, but the second verb, the one that expresses the purpose, maintains its infinitive form.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I have to write a paper about programming for tomorrow.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I understand, but I want to know more technically what programming is.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Both specialists and non-specialists are able to program.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Possessive Adjectives: My - Your - Our  in Simple Present Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You can use the possessive adjectives to express that something belongs to someone. Possessive adjectives specify the owner.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are eight possessive adjectives in English, one for each subject pronoun. They are called adjectives because they modify nouns, so you always place them before nouns like things, animals, and people. </br></br>  For example: </br> <strong>My</strong> computers</br> <strong>Your </strong>program</br> <strong>Our </strong>classroom</br></br>  Remember that you can use possessive adjectives with the simple present. </br></br>  Example:</br> I like <strong>your algorithm</strong>! It's amazing! </br>                 <strong>My mother</strong> is a famous software programmer. </br>                 <strong>Her new job</strong> at IBM  is very interesting</br></br>  Look at the chart of possessive adjectives. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"SUBJECT PRONOUN\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"POSSESSIVE ADJECTIVES\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"My\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Your\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"His\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"She\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Her\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Its\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"we\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Our\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Your\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"They\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Their\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I'm reading my textbook about programming, but the author doesn't define clearly what programming is.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The act of setting a language for your smartphone involves programming.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Depending on your design, you use a particular kind of language. ", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "social-media ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "application and virtual tools that permit the interaction with other people on internet", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  For example, social-media application programmers use more complex languages, thus to ease the use of the application.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "non-specialists", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who is not professional or knowledgeable about a specific field", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Both specialists and non-specialists are able to program.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "lengthen", "type": "name"}, {"content": "To expand: to make larger", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  There are many postures related to the concept of programming, but the best definition is that programming is the action of lengthening, modifying, and generating the functionality of system.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "technical ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "related to the mechanical or industrial crafts", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adejective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Programming involves both a scientific part and a technical part.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "broadly", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in this case, in general words", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  This is broadly the definition of programming.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "knowledge", "type": "name"}, {"content": "all what you know", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: System programmers don't interfere directly with end users, so they have more knowledge of core languages and technical aspects.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "enpe7n2le01ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Look for extra information about computer programming. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Design and create a concept map explaining what computer programming is and its characteristics with your own words. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write sentences about programming using the simple present, the verbs with infinitives and the possessive adjectives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your concept map with your classmates, and tell them the sentences you wrote. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I research about computer programming and its characteristics. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I make a concept map to explain what computer programming is with my own words. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write sentences in simple present bout programming.  ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my concept map and discuss it with classmates.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Types of Computer Programmers", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "There are different types of programmers in the systems field. Those software careers vary in the programming languages they use, the purposes they aim, and the relationships they maintain with other colleagues. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<strong>Application Programmers</strong></br></br> Application programmers write programs for common people to use. They have to use high-level languages that are closer to the English language than to the binary computers' \u201cunderstanding\u201d. </br></br>  <strong>System Programmers</strong></br></br> System programmers write programs and codes for operating system software; for that reason, they have less contact with end users than application programmers. As system programmers use core languages closer to the binary code, they have to be more knowledgeable about technical matters. ", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}]}